./ R 01134000 01135000 $ 01134100 100                                           
*  MVI 0(R1),0 CLEARED BYTE 0 AND THE NI KEPT TWO FLAGS THAT   XA0036DK         
*  SHARED BYTE 1. PAGINV IS IN BYTE 2 AND PAGREF IN BYTE 3,    XA0036DK         
*  SO PAGREF IS SAVED FIRST AND THE FRAME ADDRESS IS CLEARED   XA0036DK         
*  AS TWO BYTES PLUS THE HIGH NIBBLE OF BYTE 2 -- THE NI DOES  XA0036DK         
*  THAT NIBBLE AND KEEPS I. AN XC OF THREE BYTES TOOK THE I    XA0036DK         
*  BIT WITH IT, AND A PTE OF 00000001 IS REAL FRAME 0, VALID:  XA0036DK         
*  THE GUEST WROTE CP'S PSA. I-240.                            XA0036DK         
         NI    3(R1),PAGREF   RETAINING THIS FLAG              XA0036DK         
         XC    0(2,R1),0(R1)  SET PTE ADDRESS -> 0,            XA0036DK         
         NI    2(R1),PAGINV   RETAINING THIS ONE (I-240)       XA0036DK         
./ R 01350130          $ 01350140 010                                           
         SLL   R0,2           MULTIPLY BY 4 FOR PTE SIZE       XA0036DK         
./ R 01350175          $ 01350185 010                                           
         SL    R1,=A(PAGPFRA-PAGSTMP) BACK UP TO HEADER        XA0036DK         
